"id": "imperfect",
"el": "Ο παρατατικός",
"title": "The imperfect and aspect in the past",
"span": "A2–B1",
"blurb": "How to form the imperfect (έγραφα, μιλούσα, έλεγα), and how to choose between \"I was doing / used to do\" and \"I did\": background, habits, interruptions and polite requests.",
"intro": [
{
"p": "Greek has two simple past tenses. The **aorist** (έγραψα) sees an event as one finished whole. The **imperfect** (έγραφα) sees it from inside, as something going on or repeated: \"I was writing\", \"I used to write\", \"I would write (every day)\". English often blurs the two; Greek makes you choose."
},
